file:core/continuity.ts | the handoff note (brief) and the session packet: written for the next session's Claude (pasted or saved), English by rule; the chat answers (the story, the off line) are in the table
# What scripts/check-strings.sh never asks to translate (model names, file names, numbers and a session's own name stay as they are).
# One entry per line, a reason after " | ":
#   file:<path under mods/cockpit/hooks>   every literal in that file, or in that folder when the path ends with /
#   text:<exact text>                       one literal
#   re:<regular expression>                 every literal it matches
#   built:<row name, or area. for a whole area>  a row put together from parts at run time, so its English is not a literal in the code
# English on purpose for one text in a code file (a slash menu hint, a plain answer of a slash command, a note to Claude): end its line with `// en-only: <reason>`,
# or put that comment alone on the line above. Prefer that to a file: line here, which hides every text of the file.
# Keep it short: a text a person reads in the pane, the band, a toast or on the phone belongs in the table, not here.
re:^(Opus|Sonnet|Haiku|Fable)( [0-9.]+)?( \(.*\))?$ | model names are never translated
re:^claude-[a-z0-9-]+$ | model ids
# ---- (Settings, Help, guide, Arrange, flip faces, pop out, phone): English by rule
re:^(See every row|Change one|Layouts|Use): /vaken-settings | the text twin of /vaken-settings
text:Vaken settings | the text twin of /vaken-settings
re:^(See what one would change|It would change|This session has no project folder|Careful, Balanced, Thrifty) | the text twin of /vaken-settings preset
re:^(Tells you only what needs you\. No nudges|Balanced, plus the checks and the safe extras\. Never|For people who do not code) | a preset's about line in the text twin; the Settings view reads settings.* by name
re:^Run a command from the last answer | the slash menu description of /vaken-help run do (English)
re:^The person is on a phone\. | a line added to Claude's system prompt, never shown
re:according to | a pattern that finds text copied from outside, not a text
re:\(\?:the\|a\|that\) | a pattern that finds text copied from outside, not a text
text:Bash | a tool name
text:Skill | a tool name
text:shell commands, file edits, tools from other apps, agents, web fetches and skills | what Halt stops, in the text twin of /vaken-pause and /vaken-guard (English by rule, core/lang.ts)
text:npm test | a command a person types
text:ran too long and was stopped | part of the note that goes to Claude after /vaken-help run do tell
text:could not be started | part of the note that goes to Claude after /vaken-help run do tell
text:Vaken | the product name, first word of the phone hello
re:^(Usage and cost|Is the work good\?|Sessions and memory|Team and machine|Keeping it healthy)$ | group headings of the English /vaken-help text twin
re:^(what needs you now|this list; add a word to find a topic|see or change a setting|your plan limits, cost and budget|compact the session|is the work ready to ship|risky steps that were held, and let one through|stop every change now|rules for when you are away|put files back as they were|run a list of tasks with agents|today in a few lines|find a session by words|what a line, error or decision means|what Claude remembers|first steps|what you spend, and how to spend less|check that the work is right|hold, stop and undo|find, recap and hand over|agents, branches and your computer|look at the quality of a web page|better prompts and plainer answers|vaken itself|tools for the people who build vaken; not for daily use)$ | the words of the English /vaken-help text twin (the commands a person uses, and what each group is for)
text:Detail per card | a group id of hidden rows, never drawn
re:^(Language|Menus and help pages\. Chat answers stay English\.|Like the Mac|English|Svenska|Motion|Reduced stops the pulsing dot\.|Reduced)$ | hidden rows (look.language, look.motion): only the English text twin lists them
re:^(Cards with a problem move up; quiet ones shrink to one line\.|Suggest, watch only \(notes the moments\), or compact by itself when idle\.|Adds goal, branch, next steps, edited files and failing checks to every compaction\.|Stops a long break from making your next answer cost more\.|Stops Claude from trying a failing step again and again\.|Which checks also write a note to Claude\. Safety notes always do\.|A short notice in the session when your phone joins\.)$ | a row's first note, replaced at load by its settings.* row (core/settingsmap.ts NOTES)
re:^[A-Z]{2,}( [A-Z]{2,})*$ | short upper-case marks such as CI or PR
# The pane cards: English by rule (the text twin of a slash command, text that Claude reads, programs that are run), or not a text a person reads.
file:core/awakehold.ts | the PowerShell program that holds the PC awake
file:core/talk.ts | the better prompt, which is sent to Claude in English
file:core/setupcard.ts | the helper files and instructions that are written to disk for Claude (the card's words are in the table)
text:Weekly · all models | the key of a plan window (core/pace.ts), not shown as it is
text:5-hour limit | the key of a plan window, not shown as it is
text:all models | the key of a plan window, not shown as it is
text:Refused | the start of a ledger title that is matched, not shown
text:echo $PPID | a shell command
text:start anyway | an argument of the /vaken-tasks command
text:Plan limit not reported yet | the band's plan chip (step 2b)
text:Plan limits: not reported yet. | the text twin of /vaken
text:New here? Vaken asks 5 short questions at the first start: how much to tell you, risky steps, spending, how Claude works with you and long chats. The recommended answers are preselected. "Run setup again" in the Start questions card in Settings asks them again. | the text twin of /vaken
text:Read | the name of a Claude Code tool
text:Grep | the name of a Claude Code tool
text:Glob | the name of a Claude Code tool
text:Write | the name of a Claude Code tool
re:^ ?Plan first, then work\.$ | part of a task sent to a helper agent, which reads English
text:the current goal | part of the instruction that is sent to Claude when the chat is compacted
text:the tests | part of the better prompt, sent to Claude
text:this branch | the branch name in the result of /vaken-ship ci-fix
text:Pull requests: the PR check is off. /vaken-settings crew.pr on turns it on. | the text twin of /vaken
text:gh answered with something unexpected | an error kept with the pull request answer, shown by /vaken-ship pr
text:gh did not answer in time | an error kept with the pull request answer, shown by /vaken-ship pr
text:gh pr checks | a command that is run
text:managed-by: vaken | the mark that is written in the helper files
text:Compact now pressed | a line in the probe log, not shown
text:To set the goal by typing: /vaken-tasks goal <one sentence>. | the text of /vaken (the typed way to set a goal; the pane has the Add a task box)
text:No end seen: vaken saw the agent start but not stop. | the text twin of /vaken-tasks agents-board
re:^Computer: (nothing read yet|the computer reading is off) | the text twin of /vaken-help run laptop
text:less than a minute | the text twin of /vaken-help run awake
re:^(PR and checks: off|Not checked on GitHub yet\. gh|gh did not answer, so|Main is (red|green)\.) | the text twin of /vaken-ship pr

